# Ghost Quarter: "target land" is any land, so Bot1 may destroy its own nonbasic Tundra; its controller (Bot1) then
# fetches. The search is for "a basic land card": a Plains is found, while the Tundra still in the library (a nonbasic
# land with basic land types) may not be (`! Bot1.Search(Tundra)`). The new land enters untapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Ghost Quarter
Tundra
Island x5
Island x2
Tundra
Plains
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ghost Quarter.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Tundra.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Ghost Quarter.Activate(Ability: Destroy; Bot1.Battlefield.Tundra)
Bot1.Accept
! Bot1.Search(Tundra)
Bot1.Search(Plains)

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Tundra; Ghost Quarter
Bot1.Battlefield = Plains
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Tapped = false
